 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? You' using too much moisturizer, and not enough prime. Try using a base with your moisturizer, and thin prime with your skin milk. Roughly how wet is it? Wet your finger bowl of water, and wipe it right on top of the prime. Most people use way too much prime. Use the right base for the prime, and mix directly on top of that. A light skin uses a thin layer of prime, so it looks natural. Mix enough for several days, so you never run out. A clean brush keeps the top fresh. You' probably using a flat light that highlights the bulbousness. Try a soft box, or step towards the window.",
